Subject: [PATCH] V2f: all endpoint branches and the marginal Gram entry J_T[1,
 1] (eighteenth pair)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Proves exact integrals of every block U^m (L − S)^n over the four branch
cells of a piece (signed boxTri cells), every piece of V2b's
decomposition in closed form (two aggregates, and one aggregate for the
stratum R = ∅), V2b's inclusion–exclusion with a stratum-dependent
integrand, and J_T(1) = jtSum N g L τ C 2 0 for every N ≥ 1 and data with
0 ≤ g ≤ C(1), C(N) < N g. At Table 3 a kernel certificate (133 pieces)
gives the marginal Gram entry J_T[gen 0 ∅, gen 0 ∅] ≈ 1.11935 × 10⁻⁵⁵ as an
explicit rational, in V2d's J_T form and Definition 4.6's marginal form.
Adds Comparator/marginal_entry_v2f.json, the certificate generator,
controls, the result record and the updated V2e roadmap.

